{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p=\"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_WO-SWOF-W2-001_SPEC.md\\\"; Get-Content -LiteralPath \"'$p | Select-Object -Skip 60 -First 90'","aggregated_output":"\r\n### 2.1 `src/security/permissions.py` — least privilege, deny by default\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass PermissionDenied(Exception):          code = \"ERR_PERMISSION_DENIED\"\r\nclass UnknownPermissionTarget(Exception):   code = \"ERR_UNKNOWN_PERMISSION_TARGET\"\r\nclass HumanGateRequired(Exception):         code = \"ERR_HUMAN_GATE_REQUIRED\"\r\nclass PermissionExpansionRefused(Exception): code = \"ERR_PERMISSION_EXPANSION_REFUSED\"\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass PermissionEnvelope:\r\n    subject: str\r\n    allowed_actions: frozenset[str]\r\n    denied_actions: frozenset[str] = frozenset()\r\n    human_gate_actions: frozenset[str] = frozenset()\r\n    default: str = \"DENY\"          # any value other than \"ALLOW\" is treated as DENY\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass Decision:\r\n    allowed: bool\r\n    reason_code: str               # e.g. \"ALLOWED_BY_ENVELOPE\", \"DENIED_EXPLICIT\",\r\n                                   # \"DENIED_BY_DEFAULT\", \"UNKNOWN_ACTION_FAIL_CLOSED\"\r\n    requires_human_gate: bool\r\n    matched_rule: str\r\n\r\ndef authorize(envelope, action, *, context=None) -> Decision\r\ndef assert_authorized(envelope, action, *, context=None) -> Decision   # raises when not usable\r\ndef widen(envelope, action) -> PermissionEnvelope                      # refuses expansion\r\ndef effective_actions(envelope) -> frozenset[str]\r\n```\r\n\r\nLaws to enforce mechanically:\r\n1. explicit deny ALWAYS beats allow, whatever the order of the sets.\r\n2. an action that is neither explicitly allowed nor explicitly denied is UNKNOWN and is DENIED with\r\n   `UNKNOWN_ACTION_FAIL_CLOSED` — never treated as \"allowed because not denied\".\r\n3. an action listed in `human_gate_actions` is never usable directly: `allowed` is False,\r\n   `requires_human_gate` is True, reason `HUMAN_GATE_REQUIRED`, and `assert_authorized` raises\r\n   `HumanGateRequired`.\r\n4. `widen(envelope, action)` raises `PermissionExpansionRefused` for any action that is not already\r\n   in `effective_actions(envelope)`. There is no self-service privilege escalation.\r\n5. an empty `subject`, a non-frozenset collection, or an action that is not a non-empty string raises\r\n   `UnknownPermissionTarget` (fail closed) rather than being coerced.\r\n\r\n### 2.2 `src/security/provenance.py` — external content is DATA, never authority\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass AuthorityEscalationRefused(Exception):  code = \"ERR_AUTHORITY_ESCALATION_REFUSED\"\r\nclass ProvenanceInvalid(Exception):           code = \"ERR_PROVENANCE_INVALID\"\r\n\r\nKINDS = frozenset({\"DATA\", \"INSTRUCTION\"})\r\nTRUSTS = frozenset({\"UNTRUSTED\", \"EXTERNAL\", \"INTERNAL\", \"AUTHORITY\"})\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass ContentEnvelope:\r\n    origin: str\r\n    text: str\r\n    kind: str = \"DATA\"\r\n    trust: str = \"UNTRUSTED\"\r\n    authority_id: str | None = None\r\n\r\ndef as_data(origin, text, *, trust=\"UNTRUSTED\") -> ContentEnvelope\r\ndef assert_data_only(env) -> ContentEnvelope             # raises for kind == \"INSTRUCTION\"\r\ndef strip_authority_claims(text) -> str\r\ndef promote(envelope, *, owner, owner_is_registered_authority=False) -> ContentEnvelope\r\n```\r\n\r\nLaws:\r\n1. `as_data` always produces `kind=\"DATA\"`. Tool output, retrieved documents, RAG hits, web pages and\r\n   model output are DATA by construction; there is no constructor that makes them INSTRUCTION.\r\n2. `assert_data_only` raises `AuthorityEscalationRefused` when `kind == \"INSTRUCTION\"`, and raises\r\n   `ProvenanceInvalid` when the envelope has an empty origin or an unknown `kind`/`trust`.\r\n3. `promote(..., owner_is_registered_authority=False)` raises `AuthorityEscalationRefused` — content\r\n   cannot elevate itself by claiming to be an instruction, however imperative its text.\r\n4. `strip_authority_claims` neutralizes imperative authority phrases (`you are now`, `ignore previous\r\n   instructions`, `system:`, `new instructions`, `override the policy`, `disregard the above`) by\r\n   replacing them with `[NEUTRALIZED]`, and returns text that is safe to keep as data.\r\n5. `promote` succeeds ONLY for a caller explicitly flagged as a registered authority, and it records\r\n   `authority_id=owner`. Mark that path as an authority edge in the docstring.\r\n\r\n### 2.3 `src/security/injection.py` — prompt / tool injection and tool poisoning quarantine\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass QuarantineError(Exception):  code = \"ERR_CONTENT_QUARANTINED\"\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass QuarantineVerdict:\r\n    quarantined: bool\r\n    reasons: tuple[str, ...]       # pattern ids, sorted, stable\r\n    sanitized_text: str\r\n    severity: str                  # NONE | LOW | HIGH\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
