{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p=\"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_WO-SWOF-W2-001_SPEC.md\\\"; Get-Content -LiteralPath \"'$p | Select-Object -Skip 228 -First 75'","aggregated_output":"    reason: str\r\n\r\ndef check_rights(scope, entitlement, *, now=None) -> Decision-like object\r\ndef human_gate_route(action, *, risk=\"LOW\") -> HumanGateRoute\r\ndef assert_human_gate_satisfied(route, approval_ref, *, requesting_actor=None) -> None\r\ndef assert_credential_scope(scope, use) -> None\r\n```\r\n\r\nLaws:\r\n1. expired / revoked / unknown entitlement => denied (fail closed); `expires_at=None` never means\r\n   \"expired\" and never means \"unlimited for high-risk actions\" — high-risk routes always need the\r\n   gate.\r\n2. every action in `HIGH_RISK_ACTIONS` maps to `required=True, route=\"ARTIFACT:HUMAN_GATE\"` with the\r\n   matching authority edge name.\r\n3. `assert_human_gate_satisfied` raises `HumanGateBypassAttempt` when the route requires a gate and\r\n   `approval_ref` is missing, empty, or is merely the `requesting_actor` approving itself.\r\n4. `assert_credential_scope` raises `RightsDenied` when a credential use is outside\r\n   `credential_scope`; an empty credential scope permits no credential use.\r\n\r\n### 2.6 `src/security/supplychain.py` — dependency identity, pin and licence\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass SupplyChainIdentityMismatch(Exception): code = \"ERR_SUPPLY_CHAIN_IDENTITY_MISMATCH\"\r\nclass UnpinnedDependency(Exception):          code = \"ERR_UNPINNED_DEPENDENCY\"\r\nclass LicenseNotAllowed(Exception):           code = \"ERR_LICENSE_NOT_ALLOWED\"\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass DependencyIdentity:\r\n    name: str\r\n    version: str\r\n    sha256: str | None\r\n    license: str | None\r\n    security_metadata: dict\r\n    pinned: bool = False\r\n\r\ndef verify_pin(dep, *, actual_sha256) -> dict\r\ndef assert_license_allowed(dep, *, allowed_licenses) -> None\r\ndef assert_no_unpinned(deps) -> None\r\ndef audit(deps, *, actual_hashes=None) -> dict\r\n```\r\n\r\nLaws:\r\n1. SWOF W2 declares ZERO external runtime dependencies; these functions are genuinely exercised only\r\n   on REGISTERED dependency metadata. Do not perform any network access, and do not invent a\r\n   dependency list.\r\n2. a pin with a missing or mismatching `sha256` raises `SupplyChainIdentityMismatch`; `pinned=False`\r\n   raises `UnpinnedDependency`; a missing/unknown licence raises `LicenseNotAllowed`.\r\n3. `audit` returns `{\"schema\": \"SWOF-SUPPLY-CHAIN-AUDIT/1\", \"dependencies\": [...], \"clean\": bool,\r\n   \"failures\": [...]}` and is `clean` only when every dependency is pinned, hash-matching and licensed.\r\n\r\n### 2.7 `src/security/veto.py` — a veto that proxies cannot bypass\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass SecurityVetoActive(Exception):  code = \"ERR_SECURITY_VETO_ACTIVE\"\r\n\r\nVETO_SIGNALS = frozenset({\"untrusted_source_promoted\", \"secret_exposure\", \"permission_expansion\",\r\n                         \"human_gate_bypassed\", \"injection_quarantine_unresolved\",\r\n                         \"unpinned_dependency\", \"rights_violation\"})\r\n\r\nPROXY_SIGNALS = frozenset({\"provider_success\", \"test_green\", \"coverage_percent\",\r\n                          \"policy_file_present\", \"ci_green\", \"llm_judge_score\"})\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass VetoDecision:\r\n    vetoed: bool\r\n    active_signals: tuple[str, ...]\r\n    reason_code: str\r\n    proxies_ignored: tuple[str, ...]\r\n    proxy_cannot_override: bool = True\r\n\r\nclass SecurityVeto:\r\n    def __init__(self, *, strict=True): ...\r\n    def evaluate(self, signals) -> VetoDecision\r\n    def evaluate_with_proxies(self, signals, proxies) -> VetoDecision\r\n    def assert_not_vetoed(self, decision) -> VetoDecision\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
